course: dictionary
lesson: 6362
title: Mrs and the other titles
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Mrs is a title. You put it in front of a family name, like Mrs Brown, to show respect and to say which kind of person you mean. Mrs is used for a married woman, and children often use it to speak to or about their teacher: «Good morning, Mrs Brown.»
explain: Look at how the title gives you a clue. «Mrs Hughes from next door pops round to check on her» tells you that Mrs Hughes is a grown-up woman and a neighbour, not a child. In a story, Mrs tells you the same thing about the character, so you can picture her before you read on.
explain: Other titles work in the same way: Mr is for a man, Miss is for an unmarried woman or a girl, Ms is for any woman, married or not, and Dr is for a doctor. When you see «Mr» or «Dr» before a name, you know straight away what kind of person it is.
fact: Mrs is a title put before a family name, as in Mrs Smith.
fact: Mrs is used for a married woman.
fact: Children often say Mrs when they speak to or about a teacher, as in «Good morning, Mrs Brown.»
fact: Mr is for a man, Miss for an unmarried woman or girl, Ms for any woman, and Dr for a doctor.
fact: In a story, Mrs tells you the character is an adult woman, usually married.
exercise: In «Good morning, Mrs Brown.», what kind of person is Mrs Brown? | *A grown-up woman, often a teacher | A small dog | A boy in the class | Something else entirely
exercise: In a story, what does Mrs tell you about a character? | *She is an adult woman, usually married | A young boy who likes football | She is a famous singer who lives in a castle
exercise: Which title is used for a man? | Miss | *Mr | Mrs | Ms
test: In «Mrs Hughes from next door pops round to check on her», which word is the title? | round | pops | *Mrs | Hughes
test: Which title is used for any woman, married or not? | *Ms | Dr | Mr | Mrs
exam: Sam says sorry to Mrs Hughes for cheek. Why does Sam say Mrs before her name? | To show she is a doctor | To show she is a child | To show she is his sister | *To be polite and show she is an adult woman
